\begin_layout Standard
A (parametrized) curve in 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}^{3}$
\end_inset

 is a differentiable map 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha:I\to\mathbb{R}^{3}$
\end_inset

, where 
\begin_inset Formula $I\subset\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

 is an open interval. Locally, a curve looks like a piece of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A closed curve 
\begin_inset Formula $C$
\end_inset

, which has the shape of the circle 
\begin_inset Formula $S^{1}$
\end_inset

