\begin_layout Subsection
Regular surfaces
\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition
A subset 
\begin_inset Formula $S\subset\mathbb{R}^{3}$
\end_inset

 is a 
\emph on
regular surface
\emph default
 if for every point 
\begin_inset Formula $p\in S$
\end_inset

 there exist a neighborhood 
\begin_inset Formula $V\subset\mathbb{R}^{3}$
\end_inset

 of 
\begin_inset Formula $p$
\end_inset

 and a map 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{x}:U\to V\cap S$
\end_inset

 of an open set 
\begin_inset Formula $U\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}$
\end_inset

 onto 
\begin_inset Formula $V\cap S$
\end_inset

 such that 
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate

\begin_inset Argument item:1
status collapsed


\begin_layout Standard
(a)
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{x}$
\end_inset

 is differentiable and a homeomorphism (it has a continuous inverse 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{x}^{-1}:V\cap S\to U$
\end_inset

); 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\begin_inset Argument item:1
status collapsed


\begin_layout Standard
(b)
\end_layout

\end_inset

(regularity) the differential 
\begin_inset Formula $(d\mathbf{x})_{q}:\mathbb{R}^{2}\to\mathbb{R}^{3}$
\end_inset

 is injective for all 
\begin_inset Formula $q\in U$
\end_inset

. 
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Definition
The map 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{x}$
\end_inset

 is called a 
\emph on
parametrization
\emph default
 of 
\begin_inset Formula $S$
\end_inset

 at 
\begin_inset Formula $p$
\end_inset

, and 
\begin_inset Formula $V\cap S$
\end_inset

