\begin_layout Plain Layout

\begin_inset Formula $\varphi$
\end_inset

 is differentiable at 
\begin_inset Formula $p$
\end_inset

 if its expression in coordinates, 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{y}^{-1}\circ\varphi\circ\mathbf{x}$
\end_inset

, is differentiable at 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{x}^{-1}(p)$
\end_inset

. This is a map between open subsets of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}^{n}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}^{m}$
\end_inset

, where we know what differentiable means.
\end_layout

